60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A, the Mobile Branch, seems to solve the access problem we discussed.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Yes, Option A directly addresses the bus link loss in the outer wards.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A is backed by the high attendance numbers from the old outreach stops.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A has the highest running cost risk, but the grant mitigates the first year.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A requires no new supervision training, unlike the workshop or language circles.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, the running cost overrun is worrying, but the community halls proved resilience.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the mobile unit can adjust its route if roads close, unlike a fixed building.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the volunteer register shows we have the people, but the mobile unit uses staff.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the staff are already trained for lending. The mobile unit is a logistical shift, not a skill gap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, that is true. The mobile unit leverages existing skills without new training burdens.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am confident in Option A. It is practical and meets the community where they are.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The access data strongly supports a mobile solution over a fixed one.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I vote for Option A. The records show it works when properly supported.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I will vote for Option A, despite the cost concerns, because the grant covers the initial risk.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I vote for Option A. It is the most sustainable option for our current staff capabilities.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are all aligned on Option A.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,The data supports it. Let us proceed.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,I am happy to see the old records finally guiding a good decision.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A rational choice, given the constraints. Let us hope the budget holds.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,A solid decision. We are ready to implement.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
